    <fr:route>/def-001M/</fr:route>
    <fr:title text="Symmetric and Antisymmetric Part">Symmetric and Antisymmetric Part</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Any square matrix <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> can be written as the sum of a symmetric and antisymmetric matrix:
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        A = A_S + A_A
    ]]></fr:tex>
    where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_S]]></fr:tex> is the <html:strong>symmetric part</html:strong> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_A]]></fr:tex> is the <html:strong>antisymmetric part</html:strong>.
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        A_S = \frac {1}{2}(A + A^T)
    ]]></fr:tex>
    where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_S]]></fr:tex> is a <fr:link href="/def-001N/" title="Symmetric Matrix" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-001N/" display-uri="def-001N" type="local">symmetric matrix</fr:link>
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        A_A = \frac {1}{2}(A - A^T)
    ]]></fr:tex>
    where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A_A]]></fr:tex> is an <fr:link href="/def-001O/" title="Antisymmetric Matrix" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-001O/" display-uri="def-001O" type="local">antisymmetric matrix</fr:link></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
